Z||000010||Toddster||06-07-2001||03:07 PM||||I'll never understand the fascination with Mustangs. ITS A GIRL'S CAR for God's sake. It was originally designed in the early 60's for...can anyone guess which group of consumers???<P>TEEN AGE GIRLS!!! I kid you not. Iacocca wanted a car for his 16 year old daughter. It was peppy, convertible, with a straight 6, and one GOD AWFUL suspension. It had as much performance as a skate board.<P>Want more proof, take a look at the next mustang you see. odds are that a young girl will be driving it! It is STILL a girl car.<P>The only reason it was ever associated with any performance was that Dodge and GM were introducing performance cars left and right and Ford wanted a piece of the action. So they stuck a V-8 in the Mustang and called it a sports car. The most terrifying experience you will ever have is driving a '69 "stang" with an FE motor in it. The suspesion and braking is still designed for a I-6! Not too mention that you can't change the spark plugs without dis-assembing the car. Performance?<P>Now for the present, there is a Mustangs Only custom shop on El Camino in Santa Clara (20 miles from here). I was driving my 3.1 down the expressway near there one day when two mustangs with the FULL compliment of crap pulled up (A-pillar Tach, bubbled hood, throbbing rumble, etc.) They started to race as the light turned green. I decided, "what the hell". I ran with them all the way to the next light about 1/2 mile. The looked over in horror to discover that a "near" stock Fiero stayed with them the whole way. I leaned over at the light and said, "Maybe it's your timing" and took off laughing my a$$ off.<P>One last note. I build a 351 Clevland motor for a kit car I did 10 years ago. Performance was Good but the car weighed a ton. So it sounded better than it ran. The BIG equation in racing is POWER-TO-WEIGHT, not horsepower. and as long as Mustangs weigh 3 million pounds they will continue to be fodder for everone else.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000011||DecadenceR||06-07-2001||04:07 PM||||Hey Toddster...<BR>You forgot an important group...<BR>Girls and "Italians".<BR>hee hee hee<P><BR>~*~No offense meant to any italian-americans in the forum. Any opinions expressed in this post are solely of the post-ee and does not neccesarily reflect that of the good people here at Pennock's Fiero Forum~*~||||reg||1
Z||000012||Tigger||06-07-2001||04:45 PM||||   <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by The Fieromaster:<BR><B>so if we RICER RONIIFY our Fiero we will win?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Ah HA!, here's what we can do.  Those with a lot of free time, you know who you all are    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">, sit down and photo edit a picture of your Fiero or one you can find.  Come up with as much really wierd trick out stuff to make it extremely "riced out".<P>Post the pictures here and we'll take a quick vote on the best and most authentic looking edited picture with the most unusual mods, like every car accessory AutoZone has to offer and more, then we'll submit the winner to ridejudge and see how it does.<P>Hey, I've already seen a Ford Escort on RideJudge with something like 17" wheels photo edited in, so this isn't anything new.  Good idea, just for fun anyway?<p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 06-07-2001).]||||reg||3
