Z||000014||Huck||06-07-2001||05:33 PM||||I must defend the mustang here.  Its not rightfull of being bashed like this.  I have a 67 Mustang Fastback, 289 2brl restored completely to stock, and it it mint.  At the beach, it will get %400 more looks than any other car around, and this is ricey guys cheering for it.  See guys with lowered BMW's with gold rims and tints all pimped out go nuts over the car.  Even hardcore chev guys drool over it. Why? because it truly is a legend.  A masterpiece of art, that, besides being 34 years old and stock, will still get up and go.  And the breaking? suspension? ahndling? it feels like anything else from that era.  It takes a different driving style than most people these days are used to, and once you learn the car, yes, you can still do anything with it.<P>Now, I still love my Fiero.  Its slightly modified, and keeps up to the stang just fine. I like the cornering and ride of my fiero much more, but nothing beats letting the stang go at a red light.<P>Huck<BR>87 GT T-top||||reg||1
Z||000015||kslish||06-07-2001||06:08 PM||||Mustangs ain't all bad.  But I do have a friend who has one with the 3.8L V6 and he thinks its badda$$ just because it has a dual exhaust and some vinyl graphics.  I could toast that car with my 2m4 coupe (Stangs are too heavy for that V6).  <P>However, I have another friend with a dark cherry red Cobra convertable and that car rocks.  He's got some slight mods (but discreet and nothing flashy) and I'd have to have a Northstar or an Archie to even have a prayer of keeping up with him in the straights.  However, he also never says anything bad about my Fieros.  Something I've noticed, it's always the guys with the "all show no go" cars (95% of ricers fit into this category) that diss on other peoples rides.  <P>I'm not too crazy about the styling of the current Camaros either, I'd take a new black TransAm with chrome rims any day over the current Camaro or Stang. <P>Ken S.<BR>'87GT and '86SC<BR> <A HREF="http://www.westpennfiero.org" TARGET=_blank>www.westpennfiero.org</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000016||saleenfiero||06-07-2001||06:23 PM||||I used to own a mustang and it seems anybody who's got them think they are the SH!T.  They have speed, sure, especially the new 2002 Cobra with a 4.8 to sixty.  Even the 90's ones would be a toughy to beat with alot of money invested in a fiero.  But there comes a point where you just give it up to them and say, fine you can outaccellerate 90% of us fiero guys go ahead, we'll see who's car people look at more.  And hope they pull up to a 2002 series ender super camaro or the PPE...||||reg||1
